From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:45:46 +0000
Subject: drm/sun4i: mixer: Support YUV output on DE33 for the TV encoder

The TV encoders take YCbCr. DE2 provides it with the post-blend DCSC
unit, programmed through the apply_color_correction engine callback.
DE33 has no such stage: the blender can instead work in YUV space and
every channel CSC converts its layer into the output colour space.

Implement the color correction callbacks for DE33 accordingly: switch
the blender format space and background colour, and remember the output
format so that the layer CSC setup picks RGB to YUV (or YUV to YUV when
the plane encoding/range differ) conversion into limited range BT.601,
the only colour space the TV encoder accepts. UI channels have a CSC on
DE33 as well, so configure it from the UI layer update path.

Because the conversion is done per layer, the output colour space has
to be known before the planes of a commit are programmed. Request it
from the CRTC mode_set_nofb hook based on the encoder type; the TV
encoders keep calling the callbacks at enable/disable time, which is
harmless and keeps the DE2 path unchanged.

Coefficients are taken from the Allwinner BSP CSC tables
(de_csc_table.c, r2y and y2y*2l) in the DE3 register layout.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c     |  10 +++
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_csc.c      | 111 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c    |  53 +++++++++++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.h    |   6 ++
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_ui_layer.c |   4 +
 5 files changed, 175 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_crtc.c
@@ -161,6 +161,16 @@ static void sun4i_crtc_mode_set_nofb(struct drm_crtc *crtc)
 
 	sun4i_tcon_mode_set(scrtc->tcon, encoder, mode);
 	sunxi_engine_mode_set(scrtc->engine, mode);
+
+	/*
+	 * TV encoders take YCbCr. Ask for it here, before the planes of
+	 * this commit are programmed, since on some engines the conversion
+	 * is done per layer.
+	 */
+	if (encoder && encoder->encoder_type == DRM_MODE_ENCODER_TVDAC)
+		sunxi_engine_apply_color_correction(scrtc->engine);
+	else
+		sunxi_engine_disable_color_correction(scrtc->engine);
 }
 
 static const struct drm_crtc_helper_funcs sun4i_crtc_helper_funcs = {
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_csc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_csc.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_csc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_csc.c
@@ -3,11 +3,13 @@
